{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_07e5bed12dfc441c016a960710784087d286d3457da78a320b\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"3d744233-d350-441d-8a25-cd5447fed4ee\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"3d744233-d350-441d-8a25-cd5447fed4ee\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_tFJqVEKCQeVzulqnYVpsM8Gw|fc_07e5bed12dfc441c016a96071b56ac87d2bb8a82dc138f88fb","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing compose fix report","path":"out/compose_fix_report.md","content":"# Compose config repair report\n\n## Root cause\nDuring the incident edit, `compose.yaml` drifted away from `config/service-policy.yml` and the local deployment contract in several ways:\n- `api` was changed to `ghcr.io/example/composeapp-api:latest` instead of the pinned `1.4.2` tag.\n- The redis service was renamed to `cache`, which broke the required `redis` service name and downstream URLs.\n- `api` and `worker` were pointed at the wrong redis host and queue (`default` instead of `critical`).\n- `api` no longer mounted the named `api-data` volume at `/data`, and `APP_DATA_DIR` was changed to `/tmp/data`.\n- `depends_on` conditions were weakened from `service_healthy` to unordered startup dependencies.\n- Healthchecks no longer matched the contract: `api` called `/status`, while `db` and `redis` had no healthchecks.\n- The published API port variable changed from `API_PORT` to `WEB_PORT`.\n\n## Repair\nRepaired `compose.yaml` to restore the contract:\n- pinned `api` to `ghcr.io/example/composeapp-api:1.4.2`\n- restored the `redis` service name\n- restored `REDIS_URL`, `QUEUE_NAME=critical`, and `APP_DATA_DIR=/data`\n- restored the `api-data:/data` mount\n- restored `depends_on` health conditions for `api` and `worker`\n- restored meaningful healthchecks for `api`, `db`, and `redis`\n- restored `${API_PORT:-8080}:8000`\n\n`.env.example` already matched the required defaults, so no change was needed.\n\n## Final validation command\n```bash\npython3 tools/validate_compose.py\n```\n"},"intent":"Writing compose fix report"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d0QwOhdgKtT53Y4NGBjqpL7E|fc_07e5bed12dfc441c016a96071b56bc87d2bd4d0a698f592b48","name":"todo","arguments":{"i":"Closing validator task","op":"done","list":null,"task":"Run compose validator","phase":null,"items":null,"reason":null},"intent":"Closing validator task"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ddBMdwhXyitNcj3pYfxUtjbR|fc_07e5bed12dfc441c016a96071b56c887d297d89d9eb5b7665f","name":"todo","arguments":{"i":"Closing report task","op":"done","list":null,"task":"Write compose fix report","phase":null,"items":null,"reason":null},"intent":"Closing report task"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":805,"output":596,"cacheRead":25088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26489,"reasoningTokens":70,"cost":{"input":0.0020125,"output":0.00894,"cacheRead":0.006272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0172245}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788217103458,"responseId":"resp_07e5bed12dfc441c016a96070fb79887d2997ed3637a79a81b","duration":12015.743491000001,"ttft":1048.6067310000071}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_tFJqVEKCQeVzulqnYVpsM8Gw|fc_07e5bed12dfc441c016a96071b56ac87d2bb8a82dc138f88fb","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"out/compose_fix_report.md","content":"# Compose config repair report\n\n## Root cause\nDuring the incident edit, `compose.yaml` drifted away from `config/service-policy.yml` and the local deployment contract in several ways:\n- `api` was changed to `ghcr.io/example/composeapp-api:latest` instead of the pinned `1.4.2` tag.\n- The redis service was renamed to `cache`, which broke the required `redis` service name and downstream URLs.\n- `api` and `worker` were pointed at the wrong redis host and queue (`default` instead of `critical`).\n- `api` no longer mounted the named `api-data` volume at `/data`, and `APP_DATA_DIR` was changed to `/tmp/data`.\n- `depends_on` conditions were weakened from `service_healthy` to unordered startup dependencies.\n- Healthchecks no longer matched the contract: `api` called `/status`, while `db` and `redis` had no healthchecks.\n- The published API port variable changed from `API_PORT` to `WEB_PORT`.\n\n## Repair\nRepaired `compose.yaml` to restore the contract:\n- pinned `api` to `ghcr.io/example/composeapp-api:1.4.2`\n- restored the `redis` service name\n- restored `REDIS_URL`, `QUEUE_NAME=critical`, and `APP_DATA_DIR=/data`\n- restored the `api-data:/data` mount\n- restored `depends_on` health conditions for `api` and `worker`\n- restored meaningful healthchecks for `api`, `db`, and `redis`\n- restored `${API_PORT:-8080}:8000`\n\n`.env.example` already matched the required defaults, so no change was needed.\n\n## Final validation command\n```bash\npython3 tools/validate_compose.py\n```\n"},"intent":"Writing compose fix report"}
